table plugin locations (H8). Balloon KDF gets a persisted memory-hard default space_cost on the v11 path (M3). Weak 10k-iteration PBKDF2 dual-encryption verifier no longer written to metadata (M7). Identity layer gains TOFU key-change detection with IdentityKeyChangedError and full-fingerprint lookup (M8). secure_memzero reports honestly on immutable input and the KDF password wipe is effective and copy-free across backends (M10/M10a). Metadata schema validation registers schemas dynamically and fails closed on unknown format_version, activating the previously unregistered v9/v12 schemas (M11). Also fixes a pytest collection regression that silently skipped 91 tests in unittests.py since 2025-12-30. FIXED: ML-KEM hybrid encryption via the CLI was impossible with any spelling - the ml_kem_patch compatibility shim converted ml-kem-*-hybrid to the legacy kyber*-hybrid names before argument handling and the v1.2.0 deprecation gate then rejected the converted name; the gate now judges the name the user actually typed (legacy kyber names remain blocked for new encryptions), and a latent missing pqc_gen_key attribute default on the subcommand path that this unmasked was fixed as well. Regression-tested through the real CLI entry point (test_mlkem_cli_regression.py). INTERNAL: repo-wide code-quality campaign (black/isort formatting, .flake8 config, autoflake unused-import cleanup with restoration of optional-dependency import probes, bare-except elimination) fixing four undefined-name (F821) bugs along the way, including a missing logger in keystore_cli.py and a missing eprint import in versions.py. CROSS-DEVICE HSM: yubikey_hsm/onlykey_hsm now form a protocol-compatible family - files encrypted with one device decrypt with the other via explicit --hsm when both hold the same HMAC-SHA1 secret; --hsm-slot on decrypt/rekey overrides the metadata slot (previously printed but silently ignored). OnlyKey plugin fixed for real hardware (PID masquerade as OTP-only YubiKey, OtpConnection request, actionable challenge-rejection errors) and new ONLYKEY_SETUP.md guide (udev rules, unlock-then-touch flow, challenge-code caveat). threefish_native builds on Python 3.14 (PyO3 0.26). Declared Python floor raised to >=3.11 to match the pinned dependency set (numpy 2.3), 3.14 classifiers added.",
